shmcat
------------------------------------------
This is a simple tool that dumps shared memory segments (System V and POSIX),
files and text. It might be useful when you have to debug programs that use
shared memory.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libintl8-0.22.5-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  autoconf-archive-2024.10.16-1
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gettext-devel-0.22.5-1
  libintl-devel-0.22.5-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://sourceforge.net/projects/shmcat/

Canonical download:
  mirror://sourceforge/shmcat/shmcat-1.10.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack shmcat-1.10-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./shmcat-1.10-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/shmcat-1.10-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/shmcat-1.10-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

